00:05:27,272 --> 00:05:33,272
Taking your life from ambition to meaning

2
00:10:54,545 --> 00:11:00,545
The Shift is a documentary, drama film directed by Michael A. Goorjian.

3
00:16:21,818 --> 00:16:27,818
From the creators of You Can Heal Your Life: The Movie comes a compelling portrait
of three modern lives in need of new direction and new meaning.

4
00:21:49,090 --> 00:21:55,090
In his first-ever movie, Wayne Dyer explores the spiritual journey in the second half of life
when we long to find the purpose that is our unique contribution to the world.

5
00:27:16,363 --> 00:27:22,363
The powerful shift from the ego constructs we are taught early in life by parents and society—which promote an emphasis on
achievement and accumulation—are shown in contrast to a life of meaning, focused on serving and giving back.

6
00:32:43,636 --> 00:32:49,636
Filmed on coastal California’s spectacular Monterey Peninsula, The Shift captures every
person’s mid-life longing for a more purposeful, soul-directed life.

7
00:38:10,909 --> 00:38:16,909
Himself (as Dr. Wayne W. Dyer), played by Wayne Dyer.

8
00:43:38,181 --> 00:43:44,181
Denise Moore, played by Portia De Rossi.

9
00:49:05,454 --> 00:49:11,454
Chad Moore, played by Edward Kerr.

10
00:54:32,727 --> 00:54:38,727
David, played by Michael DeLuise.

11
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
Joe, played by Ron Marasco.

12
01:05:27,272 --> 01:05:33,272
Quinn Harper, played by Shannon Sturges.

13
01:10:54,545 --> 01:11:00,545
First Shift is a 2024 American crime drama film produced,
written, and directed by the German filmmaker Uwe Boll.

14
01:16:21,818 --> 01:16:27,818
It stars Gino Anthony Pesi as a lone NYPD officer who is forced to team up with a new recruit,
played by Kristen Renton, on his next duty dealing with violent crimes in New York City.

15
01:21:49,090 --> 01:21:55,090
James McMenamin, Willy C.

16
01:27:16,363 --> 01:27:22,363
Carpenter, Brandi Bravo, and Daniel Sauli are featured in supporting roles.

17
01:32:43,636 --> 01:32:49,636
First Shift marks Boll's formal return to filmmaking after eight years on hiatus from the industry, during
which time he set up a now-defunct upscale restaurant in Vancouver and directed a documentary.

18
01:38:10,909 --> 01:38:16,909
Filming on First Shift, which consisted of a non-union crew, began and
completed in March 2023, on location in New York City.

19
01:43:38,181 --> 01:43:44,181
Despite legal hurdles over allegations of unfair labor practices committed on set (which Boll denied), it premiered in his native Germany at the
Independent Days International Filmfest on April 10, 2024, and had a simultaneous release in the United States and Canada on August 30, 2024.

20
01:49:05,454 --> 01:49:11,454
The film explores themes of buddhism, con artist,
enlightenment, consciousness, spiritual journey.

21
01:54:32,727 --> 01:54:38,727
The tone is emotional.
